16.259.m:
Formerly in the Tretā age, O goddess, a twice-born named Parṇāda,
having reached Prabhāsa kṣetra, performed severe austerity;
endowed with supreme devotion, he worshipped the Sun.

Parṇāda too remained there, intent upon his worship.
There, in the month of Bhādrapada, on the sixth lunar day, one should perform ritual ablution;
then one should view Parṇāditya—he would not suffer distress.
